From: sss <sss@example.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: session-scoped "Allow always" permission

Add "Only for this session" checkbox to permission dialogs. When checked,
"Always allow" saves rules to session.permissions (row-level, per-session),
not to the global project-level permission_saved table.

UI
--
- New checkbox appears when request has save-patterns (save?.length > 0)
- "Allow always" sends "always_session" instead of "always" when checked
- TUI: "☐ Only for this session" toggle in always-detail pane
- App: <Checkbox> below the requested patterns
- ACP-CLI: "always_session" PermissionOption (ACP clients choose by optionId)

Server (core)
--------------
- Reply schema extended: "always_session" alongside "once", "always", "reject"
- "always_session" → bus.publish(SessionEvent.Permissions) → projector
  writes to session.permission column (avoids permission_saved table)
- "always" → saved.add(projectID, ...) unchanged (project-level durable)
- Batch-pending auto-resolution uses input.reply (not hardcoded "always")

Semantics
---------
- Session rules live for the session lifetime; fork copies them (existing
  projector behavior), session deletion drops them (no separate cleanup)
- Project-level saved approvals and session rules coexist: evaluation
  merges both, deny-wins semantics unchanged

